{{-- Shown with every result (plan.md Definition of Done: honest limits). --}}
<aside class="limits" aria-label="Limitations">
  <p class="limits__title">
    @svg('lucide:info', { width: 14, height: 14 })
    <span>Read these results with care</span>
  </p>
  <ul class="limits__list">
    <li>
      The Earth reference library covers the Atacama Desert only, so these are the best analogs within Atacama, not worldwide.
    </li>
    <li>
      Distance is a standardized terrain difference. Lower is closer. It is not a probability or a percentage, and distances from different feature selections can't be compared.
    </li>
    <li>
      Elevation is not compared across bodies, because the Moon, Mars, and Earth use different vertical reference systems.
    </li>
    <li>
      Terrain shape alone doesn't establish landing-site safety. Gravity, regolith, temperature, and radiation are not compared.
    </li>
  </ul>
</aside>
